  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strategic advice on Nature-Based Solutions to the Indonesian Mid-Term National Development Plan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This assignments aims to advice the Government of Indonesia (GoI) in operationalizing the concept of Nature-Based Solutions (NBS) within the establishment of the Medium-term National Development Plan 2024-2029 (RPJMN). An integral part of this assignment is to mainstream NBS by incorporating NBS in national operational guidelines, design and specification standards for flood risk management. Besides policy guidance and capacity building, the collaboration with Asian Development Bank (ADB) provides an opportunity to put the concept of NBS in practice by providing expert advice to an ongoing and GoI approved infrastructure implementation project.This assignment aims to contribute to:i.	Updating relevant policies such as the National Flood Risk Management Strategy that informs the Medium-term National Development Plan 2024-2029 and incorporate relevant elements to operationalize NBS in Indonesia.ii.	Updating and improving national operational guidelines, design and specification standards for flood risk management according to the potential for NBS.iii.	Improvement of ADB-financed Flood Management North Java project design with respect to combining green and gray infrastructure solutions.</narrative>
  </description>
